          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mōmentum is built on moveō, \"to move\" (EtymDB): a movement, the tilt of a balance, and so an instant. English moment and momentum come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
